#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "150649f4-8b1e-563a-a774-1857d8781212" :question/math-academy-id "e-6247" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3923e1d8-73e5-501c-96b5-d6b729260d3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6249" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151969 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b3c2bc-029c-5128-8ea9-00591c6936d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9496" :question/problem "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1 \\leq i \\leq m$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a39267-42dd-59f6-b8ac-ed7821fc16e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376722} {:answer/id #uuid "5a975324-ecaf-5d66-8df0-75f6c3f554cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376723} {:answer/id #uuid "c856e7bc-cfd7-54a1-8ef8-ae24a7c41757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376724} {:answer/id #uuid "0c3e7b5e-44a8-5d51-8f84-74788533da77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376725} {:answer/id #uuid "edc5d4d4-bbe7-5aa0-b4a6-9fac443990c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c3e7b5e-44a8-5d51-8f84-74788533da77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376725} :answer-field/id #uuid "e610f67b-00dd-5fef-97e9-8909e0df6998" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0883fc45-b545-5fcc-973d-4e09e47c03b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123513" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed7f0752-4c68-532a-8a3b-834a8d0664ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376729} {:answer/id #uuid "cf957a75-fc59-5d84-9bc8-cbb256299073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376730} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb528ca-6b9b-5cc8-8e84-e77cd9b953e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376731} {:answer/id #uuid "7338ddf5-0f5b-5580-8fd2-4c0ca7f31606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376732} {:answer/id #uuid "e66b339a-bcc5-50ee-a5ec-a2d8a29d2efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7338ddf5-0f5b-5580-8fd2-4c0ca7f31606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376732} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9f246d1-bbb8-582e-99d1-af71838caa2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbf652bc-252b-5b2a-96e3-4fd1be86bff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123514" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [-4,-3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7x-4y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-4y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-4y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31509cab-4eff-5444-8686-edd3b950ee8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{j}-5{x}_{i-1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376736} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc47503-9742-56a8-986d-11413297cbff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i-1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376737} {:answer/id #uuid "01281bef-6d85-5b96-b224-de1ac1918ed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376738} {:answer/id #uuid "fffcffcb-858a-5b63-82ce-35d3ae0cfb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376739} {:answer/id #uuid "68c2bc1d-4817-5c65-83a9-91b43f986bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c2bc1d-4817-5c65-83a9-91b43f986bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376740} :answer-field/id #uuid "5216e23a-af33-5646-ac89-b01944b19085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "300fa9fa-2000-570e-a7cb-b212b66ab459" :question/math-academy-id "q-123518" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,1]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87d4a79b-aec6-57a5-bbe8-4f2a16e97813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i}^{2} + 2y_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150721} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7d87d2-828e-539a-85eb-2fab92aa1239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x_{i}^{2} + y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150722} {:answer/id #uuid "d06acb3c-9d69-53b0-a141-5a6ac69bb1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x_{i - 1}^{2} + y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150723} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c6e74a-2d75-521b-b493-ada34132b9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1}^{2} + 2y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150724} {:answer/id #uuid "152b1e58-73d2-5d67-9ffc-3f0525c08b20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x_{i}^{2} + y_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06acb3c-9d69-53b0-a141-5a6ac69bb1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x_{i - 1}^{2} + y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150723} :answer-field/id #uuid "eea8e9ff-1615-5e31-83ee-5d7bf940c1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c8c4ecf-951c-581b-b162-445523199e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-75055" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases on $[1,2]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b251e593-6487-58df-827c-e3780c8f492f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5y_{j - 1} - x_{i - 1} + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150733} {:answer/id #uuid "cadfebff-9bb6-5d6b-9f3c-13e378596cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j - 1} - x_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150734} {:answer/id #uu