pression is $130-3{x}_{i}^{2}-5{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bdfb7ee-5f8e-5a9c-a86d-d1a457369a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376799} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5c2c13-28cc-5fa2-b369-20ebd766c327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50-4{x}_{i-1}^{2}-11{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376800} {:answer/id #uuid "11a605d4-16bb-5c1c-90ee-caf69f7a747a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}^{2}+3{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376801} {:answer/id #uuid "6682dabd-c3fb-543d-a8e1-579be791f85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376802} {:answer/id #uuid "ce11633e-4e75-5d6f-9f4d-9b6a4270ac53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}^{2}+3{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6682dabd-c3fb-543d-a8e1-579be791f85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376802} :answer-field/id #uuid "b376ec5a-c581-5bf5-9bd4-5b7de3aaad46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0508c615-8739-5151-abf4-8d872192157a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75329" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,3]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=50-4{x}^{2}-11{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=50-4{x}^{2}-11{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[2,3],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=50-4{x}^{2}-11{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,1].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $50-4{x}_{i}^{2}-11{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2973e618-fcd1-5c86-a7d9-babbcac47de8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i-1}+87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376806} {:answer/id #uuid "504fd308-fdf5-583c-952a-c2d5b56b6e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{y}_{j-1}+3{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376807} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac83690-b246-559c-aefa-a1ef2a38a33b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{y}_{j}-13{x}_{i-1}+87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376808} {:answer/id #uuid "eedde51a-2c2d-53ca-98c7-f035caa643a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{y}_{j}+3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376809} {:answer/id #uuid "cc8b499b-351f-5553-b55f-f9bd9de72050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i}+87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc8b499b-351f-5553-b55f-f9bd9de72050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i}+87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376810} :answer-field/id #uuid "d123f5c2-2bc6-57ca-8a32-add52ec34b90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d9f52f9-4b10-555c-b78f-ffcc8756275c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75350" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [3,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7y-13x+87.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7y-13x+87$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7y-13x+87$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i}+87\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i}+87)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{y}_{j-1}-13{x}_{i}+87.$"}]}
